t out in sections 40(d) and 46(2) (a) and (b) of the Civil Procedure Code in respect of pleadings. 2. The use of slanderous and abusive words in respect of the respondents would also negate compliance with the above guidelines in a Public Law remedy. The right to seek relief for infringement of fundamental rights should not
